      "value": "A Point is a 0-dimensional geometric object and represents a single location in coordinate space. \nA Point has an x-coordinate value, a y-coordinate value. If called for by the associated Spatial Reference System, it may also have coordinate values for z and m.\nThe boundary of a Point is the empty set.",
